### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 02 — API KEY AUTHENTICATION & RATE LIMITING
###
### All /api/v1/* endpoints (except /api/v1/info) require the header:
###   X-ArcClaw-API-Key: <key>
###
### Default keys from .env.example / application.yaml:
###   internal key : key-internal-changeme    (name: "internal")
###   CI key       : key-ci-changeme          (name: "ci-pipeline")
###
### Change these in production via:
###   ARCCLAW_API_KEY_INTERNAL=<your-key>
###   ARCCLAW_API_KEY_CI=<your-key>
###
### Rate limit: 20 requests/minute per key → HTTP 429 on the 21st
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw running in serve mode
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl    = http://localhost:8080
@validKey   = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=
@ciKey      = key-ci-JV/qXAikcUoSCCUsqYxLvNjxW/N3KROQtawg3VRFrJs=
@invalidKey = totally-wrong-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEGATIVE TESTS — all should be rejected (401)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-1] Missing API key → expect 401
# Response: {"error":"UNAUTHORIZED","message":"Missing or invalid API key","timestamp":"..."}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [AUTH-2] Invalid API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{invalidKey}}

###

### [AUTH-3] Empty API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key:

###

### [AUTH-4] Audit endpoint without key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###

### [AUTH-5] Audit endpoint with invalid key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{invalidKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PUBLIC BYPASS — these endpoints skip auth entirely
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-6] /q/health bypasses auth → expect 200 (no key needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health

###

### [AUTH-7] /q/metrics bypasses auth → expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/metrics

###

### [AUTH-8] /api/v1/info bypasses auth → expect 200
# ApiKeyAuthFilter explicitly allows path starting with /info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/info

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POSITIVE TESTS — both named keys should be accepted
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-10] CI pipeline key accepted → expect 201
# @name authCiSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{ciKey}}

### [AUTH-9] Internal key accepted → expect 201 session created
# @name authInternalSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# Step 2 — run agent first (creates the checkpoint)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authInternalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"goal": "hello", "agentRole": "coordinator"}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RATE LIMIT TEST
# ApiKeyRegistry tracks requests per minute per key.
# Default: 20 requests/minute → 21st request returns HTTP 429.
#
# HOW TO TEST: Send the request below 21 times rapidly in quick
# succession using your HTTP client's "repeat" feature.
# The 21st (or sooner) should return:
#   HTTP 429 + header "Retry-After: 60"
#   body: {"error":"RATE_LIMITED","message":"Too many requests...","retryAfterSeconds":60}
#
# Note: the rate limit window resets after 60 seconds.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [RATELIMIT-1] Rate limit probe — run this 21 times rapidly
# Watch for HTTP 429 + Retry-After: 60 on the 21st hit
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authInternalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### This always returns 200 if the key is valid — good for rate limit testing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}



###

### [AUTH-11] Cleanup: terminate the test sessions
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authInternalSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authCiSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{ciKey}}
